.gend{break-inside:avoid;margin:12pt 0 0;padding:7pt 0 0;border-top:1pt solid #d5d9e3}.gsh{font:800 7.6pt var(--fb)!important;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)!important;margin:0 0 3pt!important;border:0!important;padding:0!important}.gsh::before{display:none!important}.gsrc{font-size:7.6pt;line-height:1.32;margin:0;padding-left:12pt;color:var(--muted);columns:2;column-gap:14pt}.gsrc li{margin:0 0 1.5pt;break-inside:avoid}.gdis{font-size:7.2pt;line-height:1.3;margin:4pt 0 0;color:var(--muted)}.gfine{font-size:8.4pt;color:var(--muted)}
.vsheet .vk b,.vsheet .vft,.vsheet .vform,.vsheet .velh b{font-weight:800}.vsheet .vt th{font-weight:700}.vsheet .gend{margin-top:5pt;padding-top:4pt}.vsheet .gsrc{font-size:6.4pt;columns:2}.vsheet .gsh{font-size:6.6pt!important}}</style><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>Study guides</span></nav><section class="hero w"><h1>Free NCLEX Study Guides</h1><p class="lead">Printable reference sheets written and checked against current sources. No sign-in, no paywall. Read them here or download the PDF.</p></section>
<div class="w"><div class="gcard feat1" style="margin:18px 0"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h13v16H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2z"/><path d="M4 19V5M8 7h7M8 11h7"/></svg><b>The whole study book, one PDF</b></div><p>All 24 guides and visual sheets with a contents page, ready to print or keep on your tablet.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/nclexsim-study-book.pdf" download="Vexcura-Study-Book.pdf"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> Download the study book</a><small>35 pages</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="margin:0 0 18px"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10z"/></svg><b>Coloring pages for nursing students</b></div><p>Blood flow through the heart, the burn rule of nines, and where diuretics work in the nephron. Color, label, then check yourself.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/nclexsim-coloring-pages.pdf" download="Vexcura-Coloring-Pages.pdf"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> Download coloring pages</a><small>3 pages · answers included</small></div></div><h2>Study guides</h2><div class="gcards"><div class="gcard feat1"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v3M12 18v3M3 12h3M18 12h3"/><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M10 10h4v4h-4z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/ai-for-nursing-students">Studying with AI, safely</a></b></div><p>What AI is good for, where it goes wrong, what never to paste into a chatbot, and a 4-step check for anything it tells you.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/ai-for-nursing-students.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/ai-for-nursing-students">Read online</a><small>4 pages · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="M20 20l-4-4M8 11l2 2 4-4"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/fact-check-card">60-second fact-check card</a></b></div><p>One printable page: the 4-step check, the source ladder, red flags, and what never to paste into AI.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/fact-check-card.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/fact-check-card">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v6l-5 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 3h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-3l-5-9V3"/><path d="M7.5 15h9"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/lab-values-quick-reference">Lab values quick reference</a></b></div><p>Typical adult ranges for electrolytes, CBC, coagulation, ABGs, kidney function, glucose, and drug levels.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/lab-values-quick-reference.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/lab-values-quick-reference">Read online</a><small>3 pages · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M8 8h8M8 12h8M8 16h5"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/nclex-test-plan-at-a-glance">Test plan and clinical judgment</a></b></div><p>The 8 client needs categories with their percentages, the 6 clinical judgment steps, how the exam ends, and the Next Generation item types.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/nclex-test-plan-at-a-glance.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/nclex-test-plan-at-a-glance">Read online</a><small>2 pages · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h10M4 12h7M4 18h4"/><path d="M17 9l3 3-3 3"/><path d="M14 12h6"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/prioritization-and-delegation">Prioritization and delegation</a></b></div><p>The 'who first' ladder, the five rights of delegation from the 2019 national guidelines, and who can do what on the care team.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/prioritization-and-delegation.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/prioritization-and-delegation">Read online</a><small>2 pages · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="3" width="14" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M8 7h8M8 11h2M12 11h2M16 11h0M8 15h2M12 15h2M8 18h2M12 18h4"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/dosage-calculation-formulas">Dosage calculation formulas</a></b></div><p>Every conversion and formula you need for med math, with a worked example for each and the rounding rules.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/dosage-calculation-formulas.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/dosage-calculation-formulas">Read online</a><small>2 pages · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/isolation-precautions">Infection control and isolation</a></b></div><p>Standard, contact, droplet, and airborne precautions with example infections, the PPE order, and hand hygiene rules.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/isolation-precautions.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/isolation-precautions">Read online</a><small>2 pages · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div></div>
<h2 id="med-surg">Med-surg visual sheets</h2><p>One page per topic, built to be scanned in a minute: color-coded comparisons, key numbers, and the priority action.</p><div class="gcards"><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#1d5670"><div class="gh" style="color:#1d5670"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right">Heart failure: left vs. right</a></b></div><p>Left backs up into the lungs, right backs up into the body. Signs, the four core medicines, daily weights, and when it's an emergency.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#1f5f6b"><div class="gh" style="color:#1f5f6b"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3s6 6.5 6 11a6 6 0 0 1-12 0c0-4.5 6-11 6-11z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/dka-vs-hhs">DKA vs. HHS, plus insulin timing</a></b></div><p>The diagnostic numbers from the 2024 consensus, the treatment order (fluids, potassium, insulin), insulin onset and peak, and the rule of 15.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/dka-vs-hhs.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/dka-vs-hhs">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#2b4c7e"><div class="gh" style="color:#2b4c7e"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 3L5 13h6l-1 8 8-10h-6z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/electrolyte-imbalances">Electrolytes: K, Na, Ca, Mg</a></b></div><p>Low vs. high for the four big electrolytes: what you'll see, the ECG clues, common causes, and the first nursing actions.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/electrolyte-imbalances.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/electrolyte-imbalances">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#5a3d6b"><div class="gh" style="color:#5a3d6b"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v8M12 12c-1.5 0-3-1-3-3M12 12c1.5 0 3-1 3-3"/><path d="M9 8C6 8 4 13 4 17c0 2 1.5 3 3 3s2-1 2-3V8zM15 8c3 0 5 5 5 9 0 2-1.5 3-3 3s-2-1-2-3V8z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/abg-interpretation">ABGs in 3 steps</a></b></div><p>Read any blood gas in three steps with ROME, see the four disorders and their common causes, and check yourself with two worked examples.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/abg-interpretation.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/abg-interpretation">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#9d2a22"><div class="gh" style="color:#9d2a22"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l9.5 17h-19z"/><path d="M12 10v4M12 17.5v.01"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/types-of-shock">Shock: the 4 types</a></b></div><p>Hypovolemic, cardiogenic, distributive, and obstructive shock side by side, the numbers to watch, and the sepsis first-hour steps.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/types-of-shock.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/types-of-shock">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#2f6146"><div class="gh" style="color:#2f6146"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 4a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-2 5 3 3 0 0 0 2 5 3 3 0 0 0 3 3V4zM15 4a3 3 0 0 1 3 3 3 3 0 0 1 2 5 3 3 0 0 1-2 5 3 3 0 0 1-3 3V4z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/stroke-be-fast">Stroke: BE-FAST and first-hour care</a></b></div><p>Spot it with BE-FAST, tell ischemic from hemorrhagic, the first-hour checklist with BP limits, and left- vs right-brain deficits.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/stroke-be-fast.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/stroke-be-fast">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#2b6c8f"><div class="gh" style="color:#2b6c8f"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v8M12 12c-1.5 0-3-1-3-3M12 12c1.5 0 3-1 3-3"/><path d="M9 8C6 8 4 13 4 17c0 2 1.5 3 3 3s2-1 2-3V8zM15 8c3 0 5 5 5 9 0 2-1.5 3-3 3s-2-1-2-3V8z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/copd-vs-asthma">COPD vs. asthma, plus oxygen safety</a></b></div><p>How they differ, rescue vs. controller inhalers, peak-flow zones, the 88–92% oxygen target in COPD, and the red flags.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/copd-vs-asthma.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/copd-vs-asthma">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#a5622a"><div class="gh" style="color:#a5622a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 9c0-3 2-5 5-5s5 2 5 5c0 4-2 6-5 6s-5-2-5-6z"/><path d="M12 15v5"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/thyroid-and-adrenal-disorders">Thyroid and adrenal: hyper vs. hypo</a></b></div><p>Hyperthyroid vs. hypothyroid and Cushing vs. Addison on one page: signs, treatment, the emergencies, and the teaching points.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/thyroid-and-adrenal-disorders.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/thyroid-and-adrenal-disorders">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#6b3d5a"><div class="gh" style="color:#6b3d5a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 4c3 0 5 3 5 7.5S18 20 15 20c-2.5 0-3-2-3-4 0-1.5 1-2 1-4s-1-2.5-1-4c0-2 1-4 3-4z"/><path d="M12 12H8"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/aki-vs-ckd">Kidney injury: AKI vs. CKD</a></b></div><p>Sudden vs. chronic kidney disease, prerenal-intrarenal-postrenal causes, the CKD stages by GFR, what builds up, and dialysis access care.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/aki-vs-ckd.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/aki-vs-ckd">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#b5531c"><div class="gh" style="color:#b5531c"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3c1 3 5 5 5 10a5 5 0 0 1-10 0c0-2 1-3.5 2-4.5 0 1.5 1 2.5 2 2.5 0-3-1-5 1-8z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/burns-rule-of-nines">Burns: rule of nines and fluids</a></b></div><p>The adult rule of nines diagram, burn depth at a glance, the Parkland formula with a worked example, and airway-first priorities.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/burns-rule-of-nines.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/burns-rule-of-nines">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed October 29, 2026</small></div></div></div>
<h2 id="specialty">Specialty visual sheets</h2><p>Pharm, OB, psych, ICU, neuro, ER, and IV safety: one page each, same color-coded format.</p><div class="gcards"><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#7a2d5c"><div class="gh" style="color:#7a2d5c"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M8 8h8M8 12h8M8 16h5"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/high-alert-meds-and-antidotes">Pharm: high-alert meds and antidotes</a></b></div><p>The medicine classes most likely to cause harm, the antidote for each, therapeutic levels to know, and the hold-and-call checks.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/high-alert-meds-and-antidotes.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/high-alert-meds-and-antidotes">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#a8436b"><div class="gh" style="color:#a8436b"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/ob-fetal-heart-rate-and-postpartum">OB: fetal heart rate, preeclampsia, PPH</a></b></div><p>FHR decelerations and what to do (VEAL CHOP), magnesium sulfate safety in preeclampsia, and postpartum hemorrhage first steps.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/ob-fetal-heart-rate-and-postpartum.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/ob-fetal-heart-rate-and-postpartum">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#3d5a8a"><div class="gh" style="color:#3d5a8a"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 4a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-2 5 3 3 0 0 0 2 5 3 3 0 0 0 3 3V4zM15 4a3 3 0 0 1 3 3 3 3 0 0 1 2 5 3 3 0 0 1-2 5 3 3 0 0 1-3 3V4z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/psych-meds-and-communication">Psych: meds, side effects, communication</a></b></div><p>Antipsychotic side effects, NMS vs. serotonin syndrome, lithium toxicity, MAOI food rules, and therapeutic communication do's and don'ts.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/psych-meds-and-communication.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/psych-meds-and-communication">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#1f5f6b"><div class="gh" style="color:#1f5f6b"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/icu-hemodynamics-and-drips">ICU: hemodynamics, pressors, vent alarms</a></b></div><p>Normal hemodynamic numbers, which vasopressor does what, ventilator alarms and DOPE, and ICP basics.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/icu-hemodynamics-and-drips.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/icu-hemodynamics-and-drips">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#2f6146"><div class="gh" style="color:#2f6146"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 4a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-2 5 3 3 0 0 0 2 5 3 3 0 0 0 3 3V4zM15 4a3 3 0 0 1 3 3 3 3 0 0 1 2 5 3 3 0 0 1-2 5 3 3 0 0 1-3 3V4z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/nihss-stroke-scale">NIH Stroke Scale (NIHSS) at a glance</a></b></div><p>All 15 NIHSS items with their score ranges, how to score the tricky ones, and what the total means.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/nihss-stroke-scale.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/nihss-stroke-scale">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#9d2a22"><div class="gh" style="color:#9d2a22"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l9.5 17h-19z"/><path d="M12 10v4M12 17.5v.01"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/er-triage-esi-and-start">ER: ESI triage and START mass casualty</a></b></div><p>The 5 ESI triage levels with the decision questions, danger-zone vital signs, and START triage for mass-casualty events.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/er-triage-esi-and-start.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/er-triage-esi-and-start">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div><div class="gcard" style="border-top-color:#2b6c8f"><div class="gh" style="color:#2b6c8f"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3s6 6.5 6 11a6 6 0 0 1-12 0c0-4.5 6-11 6-11z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/iv-safety-and-hanging-meds">IV safety: fluids, complications, hanging meds</a></b></div><p>Hanging an IV medicine step by step, isotonic vs. hypotonic vs. hypertonic fluids, IV complications and what to do, and blood transfusion rules.</p><div class="gl"><a class="btn" href="/guides/iv-safety-and-hanging-meds.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> PDF</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/iv-safety-and-hanging-meds">Read online</a><small>1 page · reviewed November 2, 2026</small></div></div></div>
<div class="gcards"></div>
<h2>Why these are free</h2><p>Reference material like this belongs in every student's hands. What makes Vexcura different is practice you can't get from a PDF: an adaptive exam that stops by the real rules, a proctored test-day rehearsal, bedside simulations, and ACLS megacodes. Students get all of it free when their nursing school licenses Vexcura, and every plan includes everything. <a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">See the full practice exam</a>.</p>
<h2>How we check them</h2><p>Each guide lists its sources and the date it was last reviewed. We draft with AI assistance and verify every fact against the sources listed before publishing, the same habit our <a href="/study-guides/ai-for-nursing-students">AI study guide</a> teaches. We re-review a guide whenever one of its sources changes.</p><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/nclex-practice-questions">Free NCLEX practice questions by category</a></li><li><a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-lab-values">NCLEX lab values</a></li><li><a href="/for-nursing-students">Vexcura for nursing students</a></li><li><a href="/ati-score-report-study-plan">Turn your ATI score report into a study plan</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Bring Vexcura to your nursing program</h2><p>1,220 cited NCLEX-RN questions, adaptive practice exams, 8 NGN case studies, an Epic-style academic EHR and a clinical instructor workspace. The school pays; students and instructors are always free, and every plan includes everything. Students: ask your instructor, or join with your school's code.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools">See Vexcura for nursing schools</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#signup">Join with a school code</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot mktf"><div class="w">
